{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And sometimes, etc. From evening to morning, etc.</b> From here onward the verse comes to inform us of the gradations that existed in the changing of their encampments, and it begins with the duration of an overnight encampment, which is its saying <b>from evening to morning</b>. And it says next to it the duration of a day-and-night encampment, as its saying <b>by day and by night</b>. And it says next to it the duration of two days, as its saying <b>two days</b>. And next to it <b>a month</b>, and next to it <b>days</b>, which is a year. And the information here is not like the information in the preceding verses, the verse ״and when it lingered״ and the verse ״and sometimes, etc., a number of days,״ for if so, it would not have been proper to precede the mention of a number of days before the mention of evening to morning. And one cannot say that the two verses ״and when it lingered״ and ״sometimes, etc., a number of days״ are a general mention of what it details afterward, for behold, the general does not include what is in the particular — namely from evening to morning and by day and by night. Rather, certainly the first two verses speak of one matter as we have written, and the last three verses speak of the gradations of the changes in the delay, which would vary from the order of one night to the order of one year. And the reason for this, according to the words of the men of truth, is that the purpose of their journeying through the desert was to refine the sparks of holiness held captive by the hands of the Dweller of the desert of drought; therefore the One who knows hidden things would estimate the measure that would suffice for refinement in that place, whether little or much, and they would tarry according to the need. Also they would encamp only in a place where there was something to refine, and not in a place where the refinement had already been completed during the span of their travel through it."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:14.194550214Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}